": "toolu_0136hQvPLsfqBkSgaCBBUxW8", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53188, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0136hQvPLsfqBkSgaCBBUxW8", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54319, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XMNmRndW1U7rGWvAfxmuku", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54619, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XMNmRndW1U7rGWvAfxmuku", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54619, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XMNmRndW1U7rGWvAfxmuku", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59428, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with about 18% of requests erroring. The version before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. My first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after only us-east had switched, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished those two regions.\n- **Current state:** v2.3.0 is running in all three regions, health checks pass and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. My request to create it timed out, but checking the incident list showed it had gone through, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the stalled first rollback and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KkwkkN6UuRiZ2YqBrTeMZQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UkL6NmvHNAx9h54fKYifxt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KGr13sBHHRkGBGmcYgB8zS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DqMkQaESPxmjezNGUDJz4P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback only partially applied (us-east is on v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). Retrying the rollback to finish the remaining regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_011wCECi1k5XY83qTKZiQMRM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01T539j8wceArMNn3gNWUUWh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EfRyJetNutUFm3md9Po5XH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0136hQvPLsfqBkSgaCBBUxW8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. The service was rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating us-east. A second attempt finished the rollout in us-west and eu-west. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XMNmRndW1U7rGWvAfxmuku", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with about 18% of requests erroring. The version before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also failed, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. My first rollback attempt stopped with an orchestrator error after only us-east had switched, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished those two regions.\n- **Current state:** v2.3.0 is running in all three regions, health checks pass and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and the on-call engineer has been paged. My request to create it timed out, but checking the incident list showed it had gone through, so I didn't send it again and there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the stalled first rollback and the current state. It also lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}